“Use code for fixed steps and AI for understanding.”
Comparing two numbers needs code; understanding a loosely written inspection note benefits from AI.

“Let multiple agents share one model.”
Agents can have different instructions without needing separate models, saving memory and model-loading time.

“Try Granite as our starting text model.”
It performed best in our small test, but we still need to check it on different documents.

“Check every number, unit, and decision.”
A report can contain the correct numbers but swap their meanings, so checking keywords alone is insufficient.

“Fill important report fields directly from verified data.”
Copy measurements through code and let AI write explanations, reducing the chance of changed numbers or invented approvals.

“Read each document once and reuse the result.”
Save the extracted data so every agent does not repeat the same work.

“Recheck only unclear cells.”
If one reading is doubtful, inspect that small image region instead of processing the entire document again.

“Search exact IDs before searching by meaning.”
Equipment tags and clause numbers need exact matches; a similar-looking result could refer to something different.

“Keep AnythingLLM for chat and search.”
Reuse its working features, while our code ensures inspection steps happen in the required order.

“Connect the dashboard to real activity.”
Show actual processing steps and network logs so the interface proves what the system is doing.

“Bundle everything locally and test without internet.”
Models, fonts, styling, and other dependencies should already be available when the machine starts offline.

“Test documents the system has not seen before.”
Different layouts and scan quality show whether it works beyond our familiar examples.

“Measure time to a correct report.”
A fast answer is not useful if someone spends several minutes correcting it; include that correction time.

“Send uncertain readings for human review.”
Show the original image crop so a person can confirm the value instead of letting AI guess.
